# Line endings are load-bearing here. This repo is checked out on Windows,
# where core.autocrlf=true rewrites text files to CRLF, but several of these
# files are executed inside Linux instances. bash fails on a script with CRLF
# endings - "bad interpreter: /usr/bin/env bash^M" or "$'\r': command not
# found" - and WSL silently mis-parses a wsl.conf whose lines end in \r, which
# would quietly disable the isolation settings.
#
# Default everything to LF, then opt PowerShell back into CRLF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# PowerShell scripts only ever run on the Windows host.
*.ps1  text eol=crlf
*.psd1 text eol=crlf
*.psm1 text eol=crlf

# Never touch these.
*.tar    binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.bundle binary
*.png    binary
*.exe    binary
